From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not reject Windows in set_os_flags

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: the upstream CMake macro
set_os_flags() stops the configure step with FATAL_ERROR when
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is Windows. This happens in the build system before any
source is compiled, so nothing in the include path or in libafni_compat can
avoid it. The Windows branch now sets no per-file definitions; the platform
settings that machdep.h would normally select are provided by the forced
include afni_compat.h.

diff --git a/cmake/get_build_macros_and_functions.cmake b/cmake/get_build_macros_and_functions.cmake
index 0097cb0..71c7f52 100644
--- a/cmake/get_build_macros_and_functions.cmake
+++ b/cmake/get_build_macros_and_functions.cmake
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ macro(set_os_flags src_file)
     )
     message(STATUS "Configuring on/for macOS")
   elseif("${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}" STREQUAL "Windows")
-    message(FATAL_ERROR "Windows is not supported for this build")
+    # afni-win: platform settings come from the forced include afni_compat.h
   else()
     message(
       STATUS "Configuring on/for ${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME}. Not sure if this will work..."
